 212:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			/** Searches for the next descriptor in the given configuration descriptor using a pre-made comp
 213:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			 *  function. The routine updates the position and remaining configuration descriptor bytes valu
 214:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			 *  automatically. If a comparator routine fails a search, the descriptor pointer is retreated b
 215:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			 *  so that the next descriptor search invocation will start from the descriptor which first cau
 216:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			 *  original search to fail. This behaviour allows for one comparator to be used immediately aft
 217:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			 *  has failed, starting the second search from the descriptor which failed the first.
 218:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			 *
 219:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			 *  Comparator functions should be standard functions which accept a pointer to the header of th
 220:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			 *  descriptor inside the configuration descriptor which is being compared, and should return a 
 221:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/ConfigDescriptor.h **** 			 *  the \ref DSearch_Return_ErrorCodes_t enum as a uint8_t value.
